5","name":{"en":"Colosseum","zh":"罗马斗兽场"},"coordinates":{"lon":12.492222222,"lat":41.890277777},"wikidata":{"label":"Colosseum","description":"ancient Roman amphitheatre, a landmark of Rome, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Colosseo%202020.jpg","heritageId":"Q26971668","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q10285"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Colosseum","extract":"The Colosseum is an elliptical amphitheatre in the centre of the city of Rome, Italy, just east of the Roman Forum. It is the largest ancient amphitheatre ever built, and is the largest standing amphitheatre in the world. Construction began under the Emperor Vespasian in 72 and was completed in AD 80 under his successor and heir, Titus. Further modifications were made during the reign of Domitian. The three emperors who were patrons of the work are known as the Flavian dynasty, and the amphitheatre was named the Flavian Amphitheatre by later classicists and archaeologists for its association with their family name (Flavius).","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colosseum","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Colosseo_2020.jpg/330px-Colosseo_2020.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q10285","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"罗马斗兽场","extract":"羅馬競技場 是古罗马时期最大的橢圆形角鬥场，建於公元72年-82年间，现仅存遗迹位於現今義大利罗马市的中心。羅馬競技場是卵形的圓形劇場，也是目前最大的圓形劇場，使用材料包括洞石、凝灰岩及砖饰面的混凝土。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%BD%97%E9%A9%AC%E6%96%97%E5%85%BD%E5%9C%BA","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Colosseo_2020.jpg/330px-Colosseo_2020.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q10285","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":22.1,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":19.5,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"pompeii","wikidataId":"Q43332","name":{"en":"Pompeii","zh":"庞贝古城"},"coordinates":{"lon":14.489722,"lat":40.750556},"wikidata":{"label":"Pompeii","description":"ancient Roman city near modern Naples, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia