rence%2C_Italy_Uffizi_Museum_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q51252","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":16.8,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":4.3,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"siena_cathedral","wikidataId":"Q282554","name":{"en":"Siena Cathedral","zh":"锡耶纳主教座堂"},"coordinates":{"lon":11.32869444,"lat":43.31758333},"wikidata":{"label":"Siena Cathedral","description":"medieval church in Siena, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Duomo%20di%20Siena-9635.jpg","heritageId":null,"source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q282554"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Siena Cathedral","extract":"Siena Cathedral is a medieval church in Siena, Italy, dedicated from its earliest days as a Roman Catholic Marian church, and now dedicated to the Assumption of Mary.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siena_Cathedral","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Duomo_di_Siena-9635.jpg/330px-Duomo_di_Siena-9635.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q282554","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"锡耶纳主教座堂","extract":"锡耶纳圣母升天主教座堂 是天主教锡耶纳-埃尔萨谷口村-蒙塔尔奇诺总教区的主教座堂。黑白两色为其标志。为托斯卡纳哥特式风格，奥尔维耶托主教座堂与其相像。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E9%94%A1%E8%80%B6%E7%BA%B3%E4%B8%BB%E6%95%99%E5%BA%A7%E5%A0%82","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Duomo_di_Siena-9635.jpg/330px-Duomo_di_Siena-9635.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q282554","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":16.8,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":4.1,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"verona_arena","wikidataId":"Q641556","name":{"en":"Verona Arena","zh":"维罗纳圆形竞技场"},"coordinates":{"lon":10.994444444,"lat":45.438888888},"wikidata":{"label":"Verona Arena","description":"Roman amphitheatre in Verona, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Italy%20-%20Verona%20-%20Arena.jpg","heritageId":"Q26971668","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q641556"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Verona Arena","extract":"The Verona Arena is a Roman amphitheatre located in the historic center of Verona, Italy. It is among the best-preserved ancient amphitheatres to have survived into the modern era. This remarkable state of preservation is largely due to systematic restoration efforts that began in the 16th century.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verona_Arena","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Arena-XE3F2406a.jpg/330px-Arena-XE3F2406a.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q641556","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"维罗纳圆形竞技场","extract":"维罗纳圆形竞技场 是意大利维罗纳的一座古罗马圆形竞技场，建於公元30年。至今仍在使用，並以其大型歌劇表演而聞名於世。它是義大利當前保存最完好的古代圆形竞技场建築。在古代，競技場的容量接近30,000人。但在1117年的一次大地震中，该结构的外圈和最上層几乎完全被摧毁，这些石材被重新用于周邊建筑。尽管如此，它还是给中世纪的游客留下了深刻的印象。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%BB%B4%E7%BD%97%E7%BA%B3%E5%9C%86%E5%BD%A2%E7%AB%9E%E6%8A%80%E5%9C%BA","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Italy_-_Verona_-_Arena.jpg/330px-Italy_-_Verona_-_Arena.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q641556","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":20.2,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":10.6,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"st_marks_basilica","wikidataId":"Q172988","name":{"en":"St Mark's Basilica","zh":"聖馬爾谷聖殿宗主教座堂"},"coordinates":{"lon":12.339722222,"lat":45.434444444},"wikidata":{"label":"St Mark's Basilica","description":"church in Venice, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Venice%20-%20St.%20Marc%27s%20Basilica%2001.jpg","heritageId":"Q43113623","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q172988"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"St Mark's Basilica","extract":"The Patriarchal Cathedral Basilica of Saint Mark, commonly known as St Mark's Basilica, is the cathedral church of the Patriarchate of Venice; it became the episcopal seat of the Patriarch of Venice in 1807, replacing the earlier cathedral of San Pietro di Castello. It is dedicated to and holds the relics of Saint Mark the Evangelist, the patron saint of the city.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Mark's_Basilica","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Venezia_Basilica_di_San_Marco_Fassade_2.jpg/330px-Venezia_Basilica_di_San_Marco_Fassade_2.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q172988","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"聖馬爾谷聖殿宗主教座堂","extract":"聖馬爾谷聖殿宗主教座堂 是位於義大利威尼斯的天主教宗座圣殿，座落在聖馬可廣場東面，與總督宮相連。最初它是威尼斯公爵的專用教堂，1807起它成為天主教威尼斯宗主教區的主教座堂，同時是威尼斯宗主教駐地。其為拜占庭式建築的著名代表，有「金色聖堂」 的美譽。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E8%81%96%E9%A6%AC%E7%88%BE%E8%B0%B7%E8%81%96%E6%AE%BF%E5%AE%97%E4%B8%BB%E6%95%99%E5%BA%A7%E5%A0%82","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Venezia_Basilica_di_San_Marco_Fassade_2.jpg/330px-Venezia_Basilica_di_San_Marco_Fassade_2.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q172988","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":17.8,"weatherCode":61,"windKph":16.1,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"doges_palace","wikidataId":"Q189883","name":{"en":"Doge's Palace","zh":"威尼斯总督府"},"coordinates":{"lon":12.340416666,"lat":45.433666666},"wikidata":{"label":"Doge's Palace","description":"palace in Venice, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%28Venice%29%20Doge%27s%20Palace%20facing%20the%20sea.jpg","heritageId":"Q26971668","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q189883"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Doge's Palace","extract":"The Doge's Palace is a palace built in Venetian Gothic style, and one of the main landmarks of the city of Venice in northern Italy. The palace included government offices, a jail, and the residence of the Doge of Venice, the elected authority of the former Republic of Venice. It was originally built in 810, rebuilt in 1340 and extended and modified in the following centuries. It became a museum in 1923 and is one of 11 museums run by the Fondazione Musei Civici di Venezia.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doge's_Palace","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/%28Venice%29_Doge%27s_Palace_and_campanile_of_St._Mark%27s_Basilica_facing_the_sea.jpg/330px-%28Venice%29_Doge%27s_Palace_and_campanile_of_St._Mark%27s_Basilica_facing_the_sea.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q189883","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"威尼斯总督府","extract":"总督宫，是一座位于意大利威尼斯的哥特式建筑，往昔為在8世紀至18世紀存在的威尼斯共和國最高行政機關與法院，亦是威尼斯总督的住處。总督宫南面为威尼斯潟湖，西面为圣马可广场，北面为圣马可教堂。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%A8%81%E5%B0%BC%E6%96%AF%E6%80%BB%E7%9D%A3%E5%BA%9C","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Doge%27s_Palace_%28Venice%29-msu-2021-6487-.jpg/330px-Doge%27s_Palace_%28Venice%29-msu-2021-6487-.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q189883","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":17.8,"weatherCode":61,"windKph":16.1,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"cinque_terre","wikidataId":"Q275639","name":{"en":"Cinque Terre","zh":"五渔村"},"coordinates":{"lon":9.709444,"lat":44.126944},"wikidata":{"label":"Cinque Terre","description":"rugged portion of coast on the Italian Riviera, Liguria","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Manarola%20NW%20Cemetery%20Corniglia%20Monterosso%20Cinque%20Terre%20Sep23%20A7C%2006872.jpg","heritageId":null,"source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q275639"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Cinque Terre","extract":"The Cinque Terre is a coastal area within Liguria, in the northwest of Italy. It lies in the west of La Spezia Province, and comprises five villages: Monterosso al Mare, Vernazza, Corniglia, Manarola and Riomaggiore. The coastline, the five villages, and the surrounding hillsides are all part of the Cinque Terre National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Vernazza is also one of \"I Borghi più belli d'Italia\".","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinque_Terre","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Cinque_Terre_%28Italy%2C_October_2020%29_-_24_%2850543603956%29.jpg/330px-Cinque_Terre_%28Italy%2C_October_2020%29_-_24_%2850543603956%29.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q275639","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"五渔村","extract":"五渔村，又称五乡地、五色渔村，位于意大利利古里亚大区拉斯佩齐亚省海沿岸地区，是濱海蒙特羅索、韦尔纳扎、科尔尼利亚、马纳罗拉及里奥马焦雷等五个村镇的统称。1997年，五渔村和韦内雷港、帕尔马里亚岛、蒂诺岛、蒂内托岛一起被联合国教科文组织列入世界文化遗产名录，1999年被辟为国家公园。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E4%BA%94%E6%B8%94%E6%9D%91","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Vernazza_and_the_sea%2C_Cinque_Terre%2C_Italy.jpg/330px-Vernazza_and_the_sea%2C_Cinque_Terre%2C_Italy.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q275639","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":15,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":5.1,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"lake_como","wikidataId":"Q15523","name":{"en":"Lake Como","zh":"科莫湖"},"coordinates":{"lon":9.266666666,"lat":46},"wikidata":{"label":"Lake Como","description":"lake in Lombardy, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Panoramic%20view%20of%20Como%20Lake%20%28Lago%20di%20Como%29%2C%20seen%20from%20the%20mountain%20Monte%20Grona%20-%20Plesio%20%28Como%29%202015-10-25.JPG","heritageId":null,"source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15523"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Lake Como","extract":"Lake Como, also known as Lario, is a lake of glacial origin in Lombardy, Italy. It has an area of 146 km2 (56 sq mi), making it the third-largest lake in Italy, after Lake Garda and Lake Maggiore. At over 400 metres (1,300 ft) deep, it is one of the deepest lakes in Europe. Its characteristic \"Y\" shape resulted from the movement of the ancient Adda glacier, which was diverted by the mountainous terrain and carved the three branches.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Como","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Sentiero_del_Viandante_DSC_6340_%2814020554463%29.jpg/330px-Sentiero_del_Viandante_DSC_6340_%2814020554463%29.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q15523","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"科莫湖","extract":"科莫湖，是意大利伦巴第大区的冰蚀湖。面积146平方公里，为加尔达湖及馬焦雷湖之后的意大利第三大湖。湖水深达400多米，为欧洲第五深的湖泊，或欧洲除挪威之外最深的湖泊。湖底在海平面下227米。湖面的特别之处为其三叉（字母Y）形状。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%A7%91%E8%8E%AB%E6%B9%96","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Sentiero_del_Viandante_DSC_6340_%2814020554463%29.jpg/330px-Sentiero_del_Viandante_DSC_6340_%2814020554463%29.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q15523","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":17.6,"weatherCode":61,"windKph":2.4,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"mole_antonelliana","wikidataId":"Q201902","name":{"en":"Mole Antonelliana","zh":"安托内利尖塔"},"coordinates":{"lon":7.69324,"lat":45.06898},"wikidata":{"label":"Mole Antonelliana","description":"major landmark building in Turin, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mole%20Antonelliana%20in%20Turin.jpg","heritageId":"Q26971668","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q201902"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Mole Antonelliana","extract":"The Mole Antonelliana is a major landmark building in Turin, Italy, named after its architect, Alessandro Antonelli. A mole in Italian is a building of monumental proportions.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mole_Antonelliana","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Mole_Antonelliana_%28Torino%29_09.jpg/330px-Mole_Antonelliana_%28Torino%29_09.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q201902","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"安托内利尖塔","extract":"安托内利尖塔 是意大利城市都灵主要的地标，以建造此塔的建筑师亚历山德罗·安托内利命名。工程开始于1863年，完成于26年后的1889年，此时安托内利已经去世。目前塔内设有国家电影博物馆，也是世界最高的博物馆。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%AE%89%E6%89%98%E5%86%85%E5%88%A9%E5%B0%96%E5%A1%94","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/MoleAntonelliana2011.JPG/330px-MoleAntonelliana2011.JPG","wikibaseItem":"Q201902","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":16.7,"weatherCode":3,"windKph":6.6,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"san_vitale_ravenna","wikidataId":"Q721817","name":{"en":"Basilica of San Vitale","zh":"聖維塔堂"},"coordinates":{"lon":12.196388888,"lat":44.420555555},"wikidata":{"label":"Basilica of San Vitale","description":"minor basilica in Ravenna, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Basilica%20of%20San%20Vitale.jpg","heritageId":"Q43113623","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q721817"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Basilica of San Vitale","extract":"The Basilica of San Vitale is a late antique church in Ravenna, Italy. The sixth-century church is an important surviving example of early Byzantine art and architecture, and its mosaics in particular are some of the most-studied works in Byzantine art. It is one of eight structures in Ravenna inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List. Its foundational inscription describes the church as a basilica, though its centrally-planned design is not typical of the basilica form. Within the Roman Catholic Church it holds the honorific title of basilica for its historic and ecclesial importance.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilica_of_San_Vitale","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Basilica_of_San_Vitale.jpg/330px-Basilica_of_San_Vitale.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q721817","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"聖維塔堂","extract":"圣维塔教堂 是位于意大利城市拉文纳的一座天主教教堂，始建于527年，548年完工。因典型的拜占庭风格而闻名于世，是早期拜占庭艺术在建筑方面的代表作。教堂里保存有兩幅著名的马赛克镶嵌画，描繪了東羅馬帝國皇帝查士丁尼一世和他的文武群臣以及他的妻子皇后狄奥多拉和其宫廷。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E8%81%96%E7%B6%AD%E5%A1%94%E5%A0%82","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Basilica_of_San_Vitale%2C_Ravenna%2C_Italy.jpg/330px-Basilica_of_San_Vitale%2C_Ravenna%2C_Italy.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q721817","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":18.3,"weatherCode":61,"windKph":1.3,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"assisi_basilica","wikidataId":"Q207486","name":{"en":"Basilica of Saint Francis of Assisi","zh":"亚西西的圣方济各圣殿"},"coordinates":{"lon":12.60581,"lat":43.07484},"wikidata":{"label":"Basilica of San Francesco d'Assisi","description":"church in Assisi, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/BasilicaDiSanFrancescoAssisiMar262024%2002.jpg","heritageId":"Q43113623","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q207486"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Basilica of Saint Francis of Assisi","extract":"The Basilica of Saint Francis of Assisi is the mother church of the Roman Catholic Order of Friars Minor Conventual in Assisi, a town in the Umbria region in central Italy, where Saint Francis was born and died. It is a papal minor basilica and one of the most important places of Christian pilgrimage in Italy. With its accompanying friary, Sacro Convento, the basilica is a distinctive landmark to those approaching Assisi. It has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 2000.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilica_of_Saint_Francis_of_Assisi","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Assisi_San_Francesco_BW_2.JPG/330px-Assisi_San_Francesco_BW_2.JPG","wikibaseItem":"Q207486","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"亚西西的圣方济各圣殿","extract":"亚西西的圣方济各圣殿 位于意大利中部小城阿西西，是亚西西的方济各安葬之地和方济各会的母堂。2000年被列为世界遗产，也是意大利重要的天主教朝圣地。这座圣殿始建于1228年，建在小山的一侧，包括上教堂和下教堂，和安放圣方济各遗体的墓穴，以及附属的修院。对于接近亚西西的人而言，亚西西的圣方济各圣殿是一个与众不同的地标。上教堂的内部是意大利早期哥特式建筑的重要实例。 \n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E4%BA%9A%E8%A5%BF%E8%A5%BF%E7%9A%84%E5%9C%A3%E6%96%B9%E6%B5%8E%E5%90%84%E5%9C%A3%E6%AE%BF","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Assisi_San_Francesco_BW_2.JPG/330px-Assisi_San_Francesco_BW_2.JPG","wikibaseItem":"Q207486","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":16.6,"weatherCode":95,"windKph":2,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"caserta_palace","wikidataId":"Q327983","name":{"en":"Royal Palace of Caserta","zh":"卡塞塔王宮"},"coordinates":{"lon":14.325833333,"lat":41.07},"wikidata":{"label":"Palace of Caserta","description":"former royal residence in Caserta, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Campania%20Caserta2%20tango7174.jpg","heritageId":null,"source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q327983"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Royal Palace of Caserta","extract":"The Royal Palace of Caserta is a former royal palace in Caserta, Campania, 35 kilometres (22 mi) north of Naples in southern Italy, constructed by the House of Bourbon-Two Sicilies as their main residence as Kings of Naples.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Palace_of_Caserta","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Campania_Caserta2_tango7174.jpg/330px-Campania_Caserta2_tango7174.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q327983","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"卡塞塔王宮","extract":"卡塞塔王宮 是位於義大利南部卡塞塔，由那不勒斯王國波旁王朝所建造的的前皇家宅邸。其擁有235000平方米的占地面積和1200個房間，为世界最大的宮殿建築，也是18世紀歐洲最大的建築物之一。1997年，聯合國教育科學文化組織指定卡塞塔王宮為世界文化遺產。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%8D%A1%E5%A1%9E%E5%A1%94%E7%8E%8B%E5%AE%AE","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Reggia_di_Caserta%2C_prospettiva_dalla_fontana_di_Venere_e_Adone_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Reggia_di_Caserta%2C_prospettiva_dalla_fontana_di_Venere_e_Adone_-_panoramio.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q327983","source":"wikipedia"}},"weather":{"temperatureC":22,"weatherCode":2,"windKph":21.3,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"herculaneum","wikidataId":"Q178813","name":{"en":"Herculaneum","zh":"赫库兰尼姆"},"coordinates":{"lon":14.3475,"lat":40.806111},"wikidata":{"label":"Herculaneum","description":"Roman town destroyed by eruption of Mount Vesuvius","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Antigua%20ciudad%20de%20Herculano%2C%20Italia%2C%202023-03-27%2C%20DD%20141.jpg","heritageId":"Q43113623","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q178813"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Herculaneum","extract":"Herculaneum is an ancient Roman town located in the modern-day comune of Ercolano, Campania, Italy. Herculaneum was buried under a massive pyroclastic flow in the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 AD.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herculaneum","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Antigua_ciudad_de_Herculano%2C_Italia%2C_2023-03-27%2C_DD_135-138_PAN.jpg/330px-Antigua_ciudad_de_Herculano%2C_Italia%2C_2023-03-27%2C_DD_135-138_PAN.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q178813","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":null},"weather":{"temperatureC":21,"weatherCode":2,"windKph":19.3,"observedAt":"2026-05-10T16:45","source":"open-meteo"}},{"id":"paestum","wikidataId":"Q329967","name":{"en":"Paestum","zh":"帕埃斯图姆"},"coordinates":{"lon":15.005569,"lat":40.422631},"wikidata":{"label":"Paestum","description":"ancient Greek city in present-day village Paestum, Italy","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/View%20of%20Paestum%20with%20dji.jpg","heritageId":"Q43113623","source":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q329967"},"wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Paestum","extract":"Paestum was a major ancient Greek city on the coast of the Tyrrhenian Sea, in Magna Graecia. The ruins of Paestum are famous for their three ancient Greek temples in the Doric order dating from about 550 to 450 BCE that are in an excellent state of preservation. The city walls and amphitheatre are largely intact, and the bottom of the walls of many other structures remain, as well as paved roads. The site is open to the public, and there is a modern national museum within it, which also contains the finds from the associated Greek site of Foce del Sele.","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paestum","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Veduta_di_Paestum_2010.jpg/330px-Veduta_di_Paestum_2010.jpg","wikibaseItem":"Q329967","source":"wikipedia"},"zh":{"title":"帕埃斯图姆","extract":"帕埃斯图姆（Paestum）是意大利坎帕尼亚地区的城镇。它位于奇伦托地区北部，那不勒斯东南方85公里萨莱诺省靠近海岸的地方，以古希臘建築多立克柱式神廟而聞名。\n","pageUrl":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%B8%95%E5%9F%83%E6%96%AF%E5%9B%BE%E5%A7%86","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f